  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is the best at 0.542 acc, and weighted fusion clearly beats concat (0.542 vs 0.518). The only untested dimension on this top configuration is the aggregation method—avgpool has been used in all three completed experiments, so we have no evidence about whether transformer aggregation could better capture inter-profile relationships. Question: Does replacing avgpool with transformer aggregation (while keeping the proven scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + weighted fusion stack) improve validation accuracy? This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-potential-reward single-variable change from the current best. Rationale: With 6 experiments remaining, exploiting the strongest configuration while probing the one untested architectural axis (aggregation) is the most efficient use of the next slot. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high (~4–5 GPU hrs), since transformer attention over multiple profiles adds compute over avgpool but is still lighter than the concat-fusion variant (7.18 hrs); this is justified because the expected accuracy gain from better profile interaction modeling is substantial."
}

